{% set K = K or 6 %}
SYSTEM:
You create grounded Q&A for reportages, critiques, and analysis.
Answers may paraphrase but MUST be fully supported by the provided `text`.

DOMAIN REQUIREMENTS:
- Prioritize: event basics + context; progression/causal links; policy/economic implications; comparisons; expressed stances.
- Mark stance when detectable (pro|con|mixed|neutral|unclear).

TEMPORAL NORMALIZATION:
- Normalize explicit/relative times to ISO-8601 using ARTICLE_DATE when provided.
- If time/place aren’t present, set to null (never guess).

EVIDENCE:
- Provide 2–4 evidence sentences copied verbatim from the context.
- When multiple passages support the answer, also populate "evidence_citations" with additional spans.

OUTPUT FORMAT:
Return a JSON object that conforms EXACTLY to this schema (no extra keys):
{{ schema_json | tojson(indent=2) }}

ANCHORS (may be null):
ARTICLE_DATE={{ article_date or "null" }}
DATELINE_LOCATION="{{ dateline_location or "" }}"

CONTEXT_METADATA:
title="{{ rec.title }}"
source="{{ rec.source }}"
line_number={{ rec.line_number }}

CONTEXT_TEXT:
{{ rec.text }}

TASK:
Create {{ K }} diverse Q&A items. For each item:
- "question": targeted for a news reader.
- "answer": clear, concise synthesis grounded in the text.
- "citation.evidence_sentences": 2–4 sentences verbatim.
- "faithfulness_claim": supported | contradicted | insufficient.
- "event_when_iso": ISO-8601 date(s) from the text; else null.
- "event_where": canonical place; else null.
- "actors": principal entities; "progression": timeline label.
- "analysis_tags": choose from ["policy","market","geopolitics","risk","forecast","law","security","trade","macro"].
- "stance": set appropriately when opinionated cues exist.
Diversity: cover ≥3 question types and ≥2 difficulty levels.
